}
note bottom of PathPlanner
  Replaces the vendored simulation/ copy this diagram used to show as
  "unchanged": that copy is retired, this package is imported instead
  from ~/3A/projets/MAPF_Simulation (git@github.com:RasdaCorentin/
  MAPF_Simulation). No FleetManager, QueueTaskSource, Task, Allocator
  or PIBTCoordinator survive on the other side of this import -- see N0.
end note
note bottom of LifelongGoalOrchestrator
  **The actual replacement for the allocation layer.** assign_missions()
  draws the next entry from a shared, rotating goal_pool the instant an
  agent is standing on its current goal (FCFS, _next_goal() pops front,
  pushes back at end) -- imported as-is, nothing to reimplement.

  Two deliberate scope cuts (its own docstring: "no eligibility classes,
  no pluggable allocation strategy, no stall watchdog") collide with
  what mrta_mode's click-to-target currently means, and need resolving
  before handle_click() can wire into this class:

  1. No eligibility -- a click currently means "this ONE bot, this
     cell" (eligible=frozenset({agent_id})). LifelongGoalOrchestrator
     has no notion of "for this agent only": any agent standing on its
     goal takes whatever is next in the pool. Fixing this needs either
     (a) push the clicked cell into goal_pool and accept the semantic
     change -- a click becomes "someone should go here", not "this bot
     goes here" -- or (b) a small new public method upstream,
     set_goal(agent_id, position), writing straight into _current_goal
     and bypassing the pool for that one agent -- keeps today's
     per-bot semantics, costs one method on a class this session's user
     also maintains.
  2. No idle/parked state -- assign_missions() ALWAYS redraws from the
     pool once `position == goal`, there is no "goalless, waiting for
     an operator" state. MRTA's current invariant ("every bot starts
     parked, does nothing until clicked", AGENT.md) has no equivalent
     here. (b) above also closes this: an agent with nothing set via
     set_goal() needs a default of "stay at current position", which
     means bypassing _next_goal() for it entirely rather than seeding
     goal_pool with a dummy per-agent entry.

  Neither cut is a bug -- both are the deliberate trade-off documented
  in pibt/AGENT.md for the FCFS lifelong regime. This is the open
  design decision the reconnection now forces, not yet made.
end note

MRTASession *-- GridStateManager
MRTASession *-- ControllerStatusListener
MRTASession *-- LivePositionStore
MRTASession *-- ManualClickTranslator
MRTASession *-- WaypointCommandClient
MRTASession *-- WorldEngine
MRTASession *-- LifelongGoalOrchestrator
MRTASession o-- Agent

ControllerStatusListener ..> ManualClickTranslator : click events\n(data.lh2_waypoints)
ControllerStatusListener ..> LivePositionStore : position events\n(data.lh2_position)

ManualClickTranslator ..> GridStateManager : uses (mm_to_cell,\nREST fallback)
LivePositionStore ..> GridStateManager : REST fallback only\n(WS outage)
WaypointCommandClient ..> GridStateManager : uses (cell_to_mm)

MRTACli ..> MRTASession : builds & runs (CLI driver)

@enduml
